/T (Unlike traditional light microscopes, electron microscopes use beams of electrons to reveal the hidden structures of viruses and atoms. This technology has changed fields like medicine and nanotechnology by uncovering secrets that were once impossible to find with normal light microscopes. Whether it's identifying new diseases or designing materials, electron microscopes open up a gate to a hidden universe.)
