/E (Furthermore, he published Micrographic: In 1665, Hooke recorded his findings in Micrographic, a ground breaking book filled with detailed illustrations of microscopic observations. And finally, the foundation for cell theory. Although Hooke only saw dead plant cell walls, his discovery laid the foundation for later scientists to understand that all living things are made of cells.)
