<<
/Title (Furthermore, he published Micrographic: In 1665, Hooke recorded his findings in Micrographic, a ground breaking book filled with detailed illustrations of microscopic observations. And finally, the foundation for cell theory. Although Hooke only saw dead plant cell walls, his discovery laid the foundation for later scientists to understand that all living things are made of cells.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1208 0 R
/Prev 1316 0 R
/Next 1339 0 R
>>
endobj
1334 0 obj
<<
/Title (In conclusion, Robert Hooke has been a crucial part in the development of modern biology. Without him we would be stuck in the old days. His inventions have led us on to discover more about human, plant and animal biology.)
/Dest [15 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1208 0 R
/Prev 1339 0 R
/Next 1317 0 R
>>
endobj
1335 0 obj
<<
/Title (They won for his incredible discoveries of the macroscopic quantum mechanical tunnelling and energy quantisation in an electric circuit. They demonstrated that the bizarre properties of the quantum world can be made concrete in a system big enough to be held in the hand. Their superconducting electrical system could tunnel from one state to another, as if it were passing straight through a wall. They also showed that the system absorbed and emitted energy in doses of specific sizes, just as predicted by quantum mechanics.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1209 0 R
/Prev 1320 0 R
/Next 1321 0 R
>>
endobj
1336 0 obj
<<
/Title (Unlike earlier versions, CRISPR 3.0 dramatically reduces off-target effects and improves delivery into human cells. Clinical trials in 2025 have already shown success in reversing certain conditions, and researchers believe routine genetic treatments could become part of everyday medicine within the next few years.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1212 0 R
/Prev 1322 0 R
/Next 1323 0 R
>>
